Package: tidykasp
Title: Tidy Design and Quality Control of KASP Genotyping Assays
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Daniil", "Ulyanov", email = "uldas1508@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An opinionated, reproducible toolkit for designing and quality
    controlling Kompetitive Allele-Specific PCR (KASP) genotyping assays.  It is
    genome-agnostic: supply a reference (FASTA, an indexed genome, a DNAStringSet
    or a Bioconductor BSgenome) and variants (a VCF or the tidy variant table),
    and it designs allele-specific and common primers on either strand and scores
    them.  Thermodynamics come from TmCalculator and OligoArrayAux, Taq-aware
    allelic discrimination from DECIPHER, and genome-wide specificity from
    Biostrings (with an optional rBLAST database or an Rsubread FM-index).
    Annotation uses VariantAnnotation with a transcript database.  An Arabidopsis
    thaliana setup (TAIR10 genome and 1001 Genomes variation via Ensembl) is
    bundled as a reproducible demo.
